Found while building the audio routes (k91), present on main before it. The jsonlog store's report sorts by_key and by_model by cost only; rows of equal cost (all zero on a deployment without pricing) come out in Perl hash order, so `skeid usage` and GET /skeid/usage list them in a different order on every run.

Wanted: a stable second sort key (the key id resp. the model name), the same in the DBI store's ORDER BY if it has the same gap, and a test that runs the report twice over events of equal cost.

